    <!--
      macOS Release Instructions:
      1. Update VERSION in packaging/Resistine.spec
      2. Build the DMG with ./scripts/build/build-distribution.sh
      3. Sign the DMG:  scripts/sparkle-tools/sign_update dist/Resistine-Installer.dmg
      4. Add a new <item> with the version, signature, length, and download URL
      5. Push this file + the DMG to resistine.github.io

      Linux Release Instructions:
      1. Update VERSION in packaging/Resistine.spec
      2. Create a tarball of the project: tar czf Resistine-Desktop-VERSION-linux.tar.gz Resistine-Desktop/
      3. Sign it with the same Ed25519 key:
           python3 -c "
           import base64, sys
           from cryptography.hazmat.primitives.asymmetric.ed25519 import Ed25519PrivateKey
           key = Ed25519PrivateKey.from_private_bytes(base64.b64decode(sys.argv[1]))
           data = open(sys.argv[2], 'rb').read()
           print(base64.b64encode(key.sign(data)).decode())
           " PRIVATE_KEY_B64 path/to/archive.tar.gz
      4. Upload to resistine.github.io/releases/linux/
      5. Add a new <item> with sparkle:os="linux" on the enclosure

      Windows Release Instructions:
      1. Update VERSION in packaging/Resistine.spec
      2. Build installer on Windows: .\scripts\build\build-windows-installer.ps1
      3. Upload Resistine-Setup-VERSION.exe to resistine.github.io/releases/windows/
      4. Add a new <item os="Windows"> with version, length, and download URL below
    -->

    <!-- Windows Version 2026.04.09 -->
    <item>
      <title>Version 2026.04.09</title>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <h2>What's New</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>WinSparkle integration for native Windows auto-updates</li>
          <li>Unified update system across macOS, Windows, and Linux</li>
          <li>Fixed Sparkle auto-update crash on macOS</li>
          <li>Switched to date-based versioning</li>
          <li>Improved markdown rendering: tables, box diagrams, admonitions, and ASCII art</li>
          <li>Cairo rendering backend for Linux with antialiasing support</li>
          <li>Wazuh endpoint agent support on Linux and Windows with Sysmon integration</li>
          <li>Smoother cross-platform scrolling for chat, settings, and help plugins</li>
          <li>Updated app icon for all platforms and reorganized file structure</li>
          <li>Fixed VPN DNS serialization and Linux connection issues</li>
          <li>Windows: suppress console windows during installs, elevate config writes</li>
          <li>Linux: Ctrl+A support, scrollbar fixes, and VPN page padding</li>
        </ul>
      ]]></description>
